# Byte fidelity is a release gate for this repository.
#
# supplement_analysis.py hashes its four inputs against input_bindings.json, and
# REVIEW.md records SHA-256 values for the reviewed artifacts. Any EOL
# normalisation makes the committed bytes differ from the reviewed bytes, so a
# clean clone cannot reproduce them. That defect was real: the bound inputs and
# several reviewed artifacts were stored LF while their reviewed hashes were of
# the CRLF working-tree forms, so the recorded hashes did not survive a clone.
#
# Store every file exactly as authored. Do not convert line endings: `text` and
# `eol` are both unset, because setting `eol` implies text conversion even when
# `text` is unset.
* -text -eol
